__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.venv/
venv/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.pytest_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Run artifacts. Policy changed after run #2: TRACK them.
#
# Run #2's parquets lived under data/run2/ and the rules below used to exclude
# the whole directory, so nothing was committed and the sandbox that held them
# is gone. Per-row scores for run #2 are unrecoverable: no per-dataset bootstrap
# interval can be computed for it, and the README has to fall back on a
# Hanley-McNeil approximation for its primary table. That is the cost of the old
# policy and it is not recoverable, so the policy is inverted rather than
# patched. See docs/DECISIONS.md, "Run artifacts are tracked from run #3 on".
#
# The rule is: a run's OUTPUT is tracked, a run's SCRATCH is not.
#
# Tracked, per run directory `data/<run_name>/`:
#   dataset.parquet         the question set that was drawn
#   generations.parquet     greedy answer, samples, verifications, logprobs
#   signals_actc.parquet    families A, C and T
#   signals_b.parquet       family B
#   labels.parquet          the correctness labels the analysis is computed on
#   judge_verdicts.json     per-row judge replies, so kappa is recomputable
#   timings.json            measured throughput
#   pilot_gate.json         the gate's own record, when a pilot ran
#
# Ignored: caches (regenerable, and large), downloaded corpora, temp files.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Caches and downloads. Regenerable, and no result depends on their contents.
data/cache/
data/raw/
hf_home/

# Scratch: atomic-write temp files and the judge response cache. The judge
# cache is scratch because judge_verdicts.json is the artifact that carries the
# verdicts in a form the analysis can read; the cache is a request-level detail
# keyed on model, qid and answer text.
**/judge_cache.json
*.tmp
*.part
data/**/*.parquet.tmp

# Legacy scratch directories from earlier sessions. Kept ignored so a stale
# working copy does not offer them up.
data/artifacts/
data/pilot/

# Loose parquets directly under data/ are scratch by convention: a real run
# writes into data/<run_name>/, which the rules above track.
data/*.parquet
!data/*/*.parquet

# results.json and figures/*.png are deliberately NOT ignored. They are the
# output of the project, they are what the README quotes, and a reader who
# clones this repo should see the numbers without owning a CPU-hour. The pilot's
# results file is ignored, because it is scaffolding rather than a result.
results_pilot.json
figures/*.pdf

# `make export-artifacts` output. The archive is for attaching to a Release, so
# committing it would defeat its own purpose.
dist/

# Model weights. Never tracked; `make export-artifacts` never touches them.
*.safetensors
*.bin

.DS_Store
*.log
core
